  "notes": [
    "CT-GEN-1: each pattern gets a second weekly exposure through the accessories (a squat pattern on deadlift day, a press on OHP day).",
    "A-2 pairs a goblet or front squat with squat day; with FSL that would put quadriceps over P-7's 11 sets in one session, so squat day carries a leg curl instead.",
    "CT-PT-2: each day opens with the mobility block for its pattern (knee, hinge or upper): 5 min rower or bike, three 1-set drills, then Shoulder Big 3 1 x 15 each."
  ],
  "notes_by_type": {
    "HYP": [
      "CT-HYP-2, L-14: FSL plus hard sets: the first compound slot of each day becomes 2 hard sets of 6-10 at RIR 0 (RIR 1 on free-weight compounds, CT-HYP-3), and the next compound moves to RIR 2-3. This applies on the 4-day layout only.",
      "CT-HYP-4: name 2 to 4 priority muscles from the lifter's answers in program.priority_muscles; P-3 holds them to 10-20 sets a week."
    ]
  }
}
